WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.520
Godom and Sodorrah

01:51.880 --> 01:55.620
How about we poison the water in the dam for our next operation?

01:55.620 --> 01:58.700
But bombs are fun too, like the time-release kind.

01:59.760 --> 02:00.890
Y-You...

02:00.890 --> 02:02.200
You dropped your purse!

02:05.240 --> 02:06.260
And the moment you've all been waiting for:

02:06.260 --> 02:08.760
General Vamp's Quick Cooking!

02:08.760 --> 02:10.930
Have you all been cooking lately?

02:10.930 --> 02:13.210
You haven't been gorging on fast food, I hope.

02:13.210 --> 02:17.280
Though I'd especially recommend today's dish to those who have:

02:17.280 --> 02:19.310
A Fried Chicken Stew!

02:19.310 --> 02:21.810
I'm sure you guys have all bought family-size buckets from KFC

02:21.810 --> 02:24.500
and had leftovers because you couldn't finish it before.

02:24.500 --> 02:27.370
We're going to take those leftovers this time

02:27.370 --> 02:30.090
and make a stew using them.

02:30.090 --> 02:32.160
Here are your ingredients:

02:32.160 --> 02:34.040
We first need some fried chicken,

02:34.040 --> 02:35.810
about two pieces per serving is fine.

02:35.810 --> 02:39.550
It'll turn out great even if you choose not to use the fatty parts.

02:39.550 --> 02:41.050
And the vegetables:

02:41.050 --> 02:43.090
onions, cabbage, tomatoes...

02:43.090 --> 02:45.680
Also feel free to throw in any vegetables you have laying around.

02:45.680 --> 02:48.570
All you need after that is some salt and pepper.

02:48.570 --> 02:52.310
First slice all the vegetables into bite sizes,

02:52.310 --> 02:55.000
cut the chicken into any size you want, and then tear it with your fingers.

02:55.000 --> 02:56.750
Don't forget about the bones too,

02:56.750 --> 02:59.260
that's where you're going to get most of the flavor for the soup.

02:59.260 --> 03:02.860
Now take all your ingredients and dump them in a water-filled pan.

03:02.860 --> 03:07.350
Make sure to use just enough water to soak the chicken and vegetables;

03:07.350 --> 03:09.110
vegetables release water when they're boiled,

03:09.110 --> 03:12.420
so your stew will get diluted if you put in too much water.

03:13.270 --> 03:16.260
Once everything is in place, crank up the heat and let the ingredients stew.

03:16.260 --> 03:20.080
Start off with high heat, and turn it down once it starts to boil,

03:20.080 --> 03:21.900
and after that just let it simmer,

03:21.900 --> 03:23.940
while keeping a close eye so the ingredients don't overflow.

03:23.940 --> 03:26.180
Let the stew simmer for the time being,

03:26.180 --> 03:28.420
and I'll show you how to finish this dish at the end of the episode.

03:33.210 --> 03:34.400
The Bon Festival

03:34.400 --> 03:38.740
is a traditional function that has been handed down from ancient times.

03:38.740 --> 03:41.700
During this time, men and women alike go back to their childhood homes,

03:41.700 --> 03:45.720
to pay respects to the ancestors and to obtain a much needed break from life.

03:45.720 --> 03:46.900
And it goes without saying,

03:46.900 --> 03:49.440
that even here at the evil organization known as Florsheim,

03:49.440 --> 03:52.230
the same repose is being afforded to the monsters,

03:52.230 --> 03:54.580
and for nine days at that!

03:57.870 --> 03:59.730
Master Vamp!

03:59.920 --> 04:02.000
Good day, Master Vamp.

04:02.000 --> 04:03.860
Welcome back, Dolgon.

04:03.860 --> 04:05.900
I went on a trip for Bon vacation,

04:05.900 --> 04:07.220
so I brought back some souvenirs for you.

04:07.220 --> 04:08.890
Why thank you, Dolgon.

04:08.890 --> 04:10.980
Come sit down and have some barley tea, if you'd like.

04:10.980 --> 04:12.820
That would be just swell.

04:12.820 --> 04:14.920
Did you fly to wherever you went?

04:14.920 --> 04:19.870
No, I went on the Tokaido line since Minami from work came with me.

04:19.870 --> 04:22.840
Well actually, Minami was the one who invited me to go with him!

04:25.630 --> 04:28.230
Are you doing anything for Bon vacation?

04:28.230 --> 04:33.580
I'm actually thinking about catching the discount all-day train to Nagoya.

04:33.580 --> 04:35.240
You're going to just hang out on the Tokaido line then?

04:35.240 --> 04:38.240
That sounds awesome. You have to go on those slow-life journeys once in a while.

04:38.240 --> 04:40.250
Would you like to come with me?

04:40.250 --> 04:42.080
Really?

04:42.080 --> 04:43.660
So, did you have fun?

04:43.660 --> 04:45.540
Well "fun" wouldn't quite describe it...

04:45.540 --> 04:46.900
Oh, thank you.

04:46.900 --> 04:49.050
It was actually dreadful for a while.

04:49.050 --> 04:52.240
The train heading down was packed like a can of sardines.

04:53.770 --> 04:54.730
Sorry.

04:54.730 --> 04:56.730
It was a good thing that I put on my beak guard,

04:56.730 --> 04:59.910
else there probably would have been blood everywhere.

04:59.910 --> 05:02.650
We somehow made it past the Kawasaki-Fujisawa rush,

05:02.650 --> 05:05.520
but we had to make a stop in Ofuna because I was literally short of air.

05:05.520 --> 05:08.660
Are you all right, Dolgon?

05:08.660 --> 05:10.260
I'm fine.

05:10.260 --> 05:12.140
I'm so sorry, Minami.

05:12.140 --> 05:14.450
I can't breathe with this thing on.

05:14.450 --> 05:17.630
I'd thought we'd be fine because I heard on the news

05:17.630 --> 05:19.250
that the homecoming rush this year would be a little more sporadic.

05:19.250 --> 05:21.400
Boy was I wrong.

05:21.400 --> 05:24.010
But you at least got to go see Nagoya, right?

05:24.010 --> 05:25.870
Well actually...

05:27.040 --> 05:32.180
This Misokatsu isn't all that different from the ones they sell at the supermarkets.

05:32.180 --> 05:34.830
I guess that's why there aren't that many people eating here.

05:34.830 --> 05:36.790
We went without consulting Yelp.com,

05:36.790 --> 05:39.730
so we kept ending up in these god awful restaurants.

05:39.730 --> 05:43.040
Why didn't you just pick up a local gourmet guide or something?

05:43.040 --> 05:47.520
Oh yeah, I guess we should have done that.

05:47.680 --> 05:51.760
And then that damn Red started beating me with a steel pipe.

05:51.760 --> 05:53.070
No way!

05:53.070 --> 05:54.760
Yeah, way.

05:54.760 --> 05:58.320
The hotel we were staying at had really thin walls like a business hotel,

05:58.320 --> 06:01.170
so we got complaints from the people next door when we were drinking,

06:01.170 --> 06:03.350
and the concierge warned us to be quiet.

06:03.350 --> 06:06.160
I wanted to order some pay-per-view porn,

06:06.160 --> 06:08.840
but there's no way you could watch something like that with the walls being so thin.

06:08.840 --> 06:09.950
Huh?

06:09.950 --> 06:11.840
Well thanks to the trip,

06:11.840 --> 06:14.350
I've become such better friends with Minami.

06:14.350 --> 06:16.210
That's the stuff vacation memories are made of.

06:16.210 --> 06:18.120
We're home.

06:18.120 --> 06:19.880
We're back, Master Vamp.

06:19.880 --> 06:20.790
Welcome  back.

06:20.790 --> 06:21.670
What's up Dol!

06:21.670 --> 06:23.820
How's it going?

06:24.430 --> 06:27.440
So we weren't the only ones having a rough time then.

06:27.440 --> 06:32.310
We drove over to the Gotenba Outlets for Bon vacation,

06:32.310 --> 06:34.630
but man were we in for an adventure.

06:34.630 --> 06:36.300
Who drove?

06:36.300 --> 06:37.920
I drove the rental car.

06:37.920 --> 06:39.390
So what kind of "adventure" did you have?

06:39.390 --> 06:41.950
Well it was mostly this guy's fault.

06:41.950 --> 06:44.560
Yeah, yeah, it's all my fault.

06:45.060 --> 06:47.900
He was more excited than all of us before we got in the car.

06:47.900 --> 06:50.510
Hey come on, I wanna sit shotgun.

06:50.510 --> 06:52.080
No way, Jose.

06:52.080 --> 06:53.560
Runts like you can sit in the back.

06:53.560 --> 06:55.540
You're so cheap, Medallion!

06:55.540 --> 06:56.850
Check it out, Usa.

06:56.850 --> 06:59.950
Look at all these snacks I brought.

06:59.950 --> 07:01.200
That's so awesome.

07:00.700 --> 07:03.130
Isn't it awesome?

07:01.200 --> 07:03.130
Gimme, gimme!

07:03.130 --> 07:05.960
Shut the hell up, you two!

07:06.100 --> 07:08.810
I even froze some juice for us!

07:08.810 --> 07:11.540
I get that you're excited but simmer down a little.

07:11.540 --> 07:13.200
Stop saying "gimme"!

07:13.200 --> 07:15.290
I can't concentrate on driving with you yelping like that!

07:16.310 --> 07:18.160
Then he got carsick before we even got on the freeway.

07:18.160 --> 07:21.210
Yay, shotgun!

07:21.210 --> 07:24.610
I'm sitting shotgun!

07:26.880 --> 07:29.740
Hey Usa, that cheese...

07:30.230 --> 07:31.290
Geez.

07:31.290 --> 07:35.330
And to think that just moments ago you were as lively as a fish out of water.

07:35.330 --> 07:37.980
Dammit, Usa, you're getting crumbs everywhere!

07:37.980 --> 07:40.290
How the hell can a monster trying to conquer the world

07:40.290 --> 07:42.680
succumb to a shaky car ride?

07:42.680 --> 07:46.690
Well a monster trying to conquer the world shouldn't drive so safely like you either!

07:46.690 --> 07:49.200
Look at you with your sunglasses and your student driver sticker.

07:49.200 --> 07:51.490
You're nothing but despicable low-level scum.

07:53.340 --> 07:56.770
Oh shit, my stomach's starting to hurt.

07:56.770 --> 07:59.780
It must be because I had that frozen juice earlier.

07:59.780 --> 08:01.030
Are you serious?

08:01.030 --> 08:03.280
That's just great.

08:03.540 --> 08:04.790
I guess we have no choice.

08:04.790 --> 08:08.420
The Ebina service area is coming up ahead so we'll take a break there.

08:09.120 --> 08:11.820
So you guys stopped at the service area then.

08:11.820 --> 08:13.150
Well actually...

08:16.110 --> 08:18.340
Sorry, I'll be at the men's room.

08:18.340 --> 08:22.080
I'm going to be circling the area since I don't see anywhere to park.

08:22.080 --> 08:25.210
Usa's going to be flying over me so just look for that, okay?

08:25.210 --> 08:28.610
And he didn't come back for a whole hour!

08:28.610 --> 08:32.220
Well it's not my fault that the restroom was hella crowded!

08:32.220 --> 08:35.020
And then a bunch of hags decided to use our toilets too.

08:35.020 --> 08:37.400
Oh my, is this really okay?

08:37.400 --> 08:40.890
The ladies' room is crowded so we don't have much of a choice.

08:41.310 --> 08:42.900
W-Wait, you two.

08:42.900 --> 08:44.430
This is the men's room.

08:44.430 --> 08:48.410
Oh it's okay, we don't mind.

08:50.170 --> 08:51.220
Please mind.

08:51.220 --> 08:53.860
Those damn hags!

08:53.860 --> 08:56.170
I was so shocked that I couldn't say anything to them.

08:56.170 --> 08:57.290
Come on you guys,

08:57.290 --> 09:00.360
it's not nice to refer to people as "hags."

09:00.360 --> 09:03.090
In the end, I couldn't find any parking at all,

09:03.090 --> 09:06.390
so I didn't even get to go into the service area.

09:06.390 --> 09:09.770
I didn't get to try their famous shumais and melon bread.

09:09.770 --> 09:11.120
There, there.

09:11.120 --> 09:13.890
But I thought you guys were trying to get to the Gotenba Outlets?

09:13.890 --> 09:14.890
Oh yeah.

09:14.890 --> 09:17.850
So we somehow managed to get to the outlets after that,

09:17.850 --> 09:20.250
and looked at what they were selling,

09:20.250 --> 09:23.050
but there really wasn't anything worth buying.

09:23.050 --> 09:25.700
I bought socks at least.

09:25.700 --> 09:26.570
I see.

09:26.570 --> 09:30.950
Then we saw a gyoza restaurant so we figured we'd have lunch there.

09:31.750 --> 09:33.860
I think I'll pass.

09:33.860 --> 09:35.300
Gyoza has an intense aroma

09:35.300 --> 09:38.450
so I might get sick on our way back again.

09:38.450 --> 09:40.330
And that ruined it for us.

09:41.030 --> 09:42.790
So we figured it'd probably be best

09:42.790 --> 09:46.440
if Usa and I just got churros from the churro stand and be on our way, but...

09:46.440 --> 09:47.980
It's Usa!

09:47.980 --> 09:48.680
Oh my god, he's cute!

09:48.680 --> 09:51.240
Come on, stop! I can't eat churros like this!

09:51.240 --> 09:53.950
Before we noticed, Usa was surrounded by a bunch of people,

09:53.950 --> 09:55.970
and things got ridiculous.

09:55.970 --> 09:57.470
Geez.

09:57.470 --> 10:00.010
We paid the freeway toll for nothing in the end.

10:00.010 --> 10:02.090
That sounds awful.

10:02.090 --> 10:04.590
Did <i>you </i> go anywhere, Master Vamp?

10:04.590 --> 10:06.450
Nope, and I don't plan on leaving.

10:06.450 --> 10:07.680
So you're going to relax at home?

10:07.680 --> 10:09.520
That's probably for the best.

10:09.520 --> 10:13.170
Actually, Kayoko ended up going back home...

10:13.870 --> 10:18.390
so Mr. Red came to the base for breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

10:18.930 --> 10:23.290
Aren't you going to go to Kayoko's parents' house, Mr. Red?

10:24.010 --> 10:25.450
Hell no.

10:25.450 --> 10:28.990
How am I supposed to meet her parents?

10:28.990 --> 10:30.460
Get me some more edamame.

10:31.490 --> 10:34.210
So I didn't even have a moment's rest.

10:35.900 --> 10:39.610
Master Vamp had it the worst out of all of us.

10:39.610 --> 10:40.480
I gotta pee!

10:41.280 --> 10:43.140
Astro Fighter Sunred.

10:43.140 --> 10:46.000
This is the magnificent story of the conflict between good and evil

10:46.000 --> 10:49.220
which takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

10:52.490 --> 10:55.280
And now, Quick Recipes part two!

10:55.280 --> 10:58.520
Now let's pick up from where we left off.

10:58.520 --> 10:59.740
After boiling for a bit,

10:59.740 --> 11:03.240
the skin will fall off the chicken and thicken the soup.

11:03.240 --> 11:04.890
Last but not least,

11:04.890 --> 11:06.740
add some salt and pepper for flavor.

11:06.740 --> 11:09.070
You might not want to add too much

11:09.070 --> 11:11.500
since there's already the flavoring from the chicken.

11:11.500 --> 11:13.200
Now kill the fire,

11:14.630 --> 11:16.910
serve it in a bowl, and voila:

11:16.910 --> 11:18.590
A Fried Chicken Stew.

11:18.590 --> 11:20.560
Be sure to eat it while it's still hot.

11:22.140 --> 11:26.620
This is an unexpectedly deep flavor considering it's made from left-overs.

11:26.620 --> 11:29.900
I'd also recommend adding some tabasco sauce for extra flavor.
